{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Variable.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Variable.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"variable variable","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Variable.md","fileName":"Variable.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Variable","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Algebraic Expressions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Algebraic Expressions","Mathematical Generality","Algebraic Identity","Substitution","Unknown Variable","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Variable.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Variable.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"variable variable","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Variable.md","fileName":"Variable.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Variable","heading":"Variable","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A variable is a symbol, usually a letter, used to represent a number without fixing one numerical value in the expression. It permits [[Mathematical Generality]] because a relationship written with (a) and (b) can apply to every allowed pair rather than requiring a list of examples.\n\nA variable can play different roles. It may denote an arbitrary value in an [[Algebraic Identity]], an input assigned during [[Substitution]], or an [[Unknown Variable]] whose value must be found from an equation. Its written sign does not reveal the sign of its value; (-x) is positive whenever (x) is negative.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Algebraic Expressions","Mathematical Generality","Algebraic Identity","Substitution","Unknown Variable","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Variable.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Variable.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearc